          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Uṣṭra meant a buffalo in the Rigveda and a camel only from the epics on (MW, CDIAL 2387). It lives on as Hindi ūṃṭ, \"camel\"."
            }
          ]
